    {
      "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@68097",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [],
      "text": "GOWER.\nHere ’a comes; and the Scots captain, Captain Jamy, with him.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@68097/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 6,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@68097/line-2",
          "start": 7,
          "end": 68,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1967526,
        "end": 1967608,
        "line": 73012,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap11/p@68097",
        "anchor": "sceneIII_11.2"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "GOWER.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@68183",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [],
      "text": "FLUELLEN.\nCaptain Jamy is a marvellous falorous gentleman, that is certain; and of great expedition and knowledge in the anchient wars, upon my particular knowledge of his directions. By Cheshu, he will maintain his argument as well as any military man in the world, in the disciplines of the pristine wars of the Romans.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@68183/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@68183/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 321,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1967612,
        "end": 1967951,
        "line": 73016,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap11/p@68183",
        "anchor": "sceneIII_11.2"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "FLUELLEN.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@68526",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [],
      "text": "JAMY.\nI say gud-day, Captain Fluellen.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@68526/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 5,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@68526/line-2",
          "start": 6,
          "end": 38,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1967955,
        "end": 1968007,
        "line": 73024,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap11/p@68526",
        "anchor": "sceneIII_11.2"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "JAMY.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@68582",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [],
      "text": "FLUELLEN.\nGod-den to your worship, good Captain James.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@68582/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@68582/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 54,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1968011,
        "end": 1968079,
        "line": 73028,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap11/p@68582",
        "anchor": "sceneIII_11.2"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "FLUELLEN.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@68654",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [],
      "text": "GOWER.\nHow now, Captain Macmorris! have you quit the mines?\nHave the pioneers given o’er?",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@68654/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 6,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@68654/line-2",
          "start": 7,
          "end": 59,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@68654/line-3",
          "start": 60,
          "end": 89,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1968083,
        "end": 1968191,
        "line": 73032,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap11/p@68654",
        "anchor": "sceneIII_11.2"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "GOWER.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@68766",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [],
      "text": "MACMORRIS.\nBy Chrish, la! ’tish ill done! The work ish give over, the trompet sound the retreat. By my hand I swear, and my father’s soul, the work ish ill done; it ish give over. I would have blowed up the town, so Chrish save me, la! in an hour. O, ’tish ill done, ’tish ill done; by my hand, ’tish ill done!",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@68766/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 10,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@68766/line-2",
          "start": 11,
          "end": 310,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1968195,
        "end": 1968523,
        "line": 73037,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap11/p@68766",
        "anchor": "sceneIII_11.2"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "MACMORRIS.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 10
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@69098",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [],
      "text": "FLUELLEN.\nCaptain Macmorris, I beseech you now, will you voutsafe me, look you, a few disputations with you, as partly touching or concerning the disciplines of the war, the Roman wars, in the way of argument, look you, and friendly communication; partly to satisfy my opinion, and partly for the satisfaction, look you, of my mind, as touching the direction of the military discipline; that is the point.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@69098/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@69098/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 405,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1968527,
        "end": 1968951,
        "line": 73045,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap11/p@69098",
        "anchor": "sceneIII_11.2"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "FLUELLEN.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@69526",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [],
      "text": "JAMY.\nIt sall be vary gud, gud feith, gud captains bath: and I sall quit you with gud leve, as I may pick occasion; that sall I, marry.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@69526/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 5,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@69526/line-2",
          "start": 6,
          "end": 135,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1968955,
        "end": 1969105,
        "line": 73054,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap11/p@69526",
        "anchor": "sceneIII_11.2"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "JAMY.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@69680",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [],
      "text": "MACMORRIS.\nIt is no time to discourse, so Chrish save me. The day is hot, and the weather, and the wars, and the King, and the Dukes. It is no time to discourse. The town is beseech’d, and the trumpet call us to the breach, and we talk, and, be Chrish, do nothing. ’Tis shame for us all. So God sa’ me, ’tis shame to stand still; it is shame, by my hand; and there is throats to be cut, and works to be done; and there ish nothing done, so Chrish sa’ me, la!",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@69680/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 10,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@69680/line-2",
          "start": 11,
          "end": 458,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1969109,
        "end": 1969587,
        "line": 73059,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap11/p@69680",
        "anchor": "sceneIII_11.2"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "MACMORRIS.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 10
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@70162",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [],
      "text": "JAMY.\nBy the mess, ere theise eyes of mine take themselves to slomber, I’ll de gud service, or I’ll lig i’ the grund for it; ay, or go to death; and I’ll pay’t as valorously as I may, that sall I suerly do, that is the breff and the long. Marry, I wad full fain heard some question ’tween you tway.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@70162/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 5,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@70162/line-2",
          "start": 6,
          "end": 298,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1969591,
        "end": 1969907,
        "line": 73069,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap11/p@70162",
        "anchor": "sceneIII_11.2"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "JAMY.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@70482",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [],
      "text": "FLUELLEN.\nCaptain Macmorris, I think, look you, under your correction, there is not many of your nation—",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@70482/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@70482/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 104,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1969911,
        "end": 1970030,
        "line": 73077,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap11/p@70482",
        "anchor": "sceneIII_11.2"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "FLUELLEN.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@70605",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [],
      "text": "MACMORRIS.\nOf my nation! What ish my nation? Ish a villain, and a bastard, and a knave, and a rascal? What ish my nation? Who talks of my nation?",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@70605/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 10,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@70605/line-2",
          "start": 11,
          "end": 145,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1970034,
        "end": 1970194,
        "line": 73082,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap11/p@70605",
        "anchor": "sceneIII_11.2"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "MACMORRIS.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 10
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@70769",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [],
      "text": "FLUELLEN.\nLook you, if you take the matter otherwise than is meant, Captain Macmorris, peradventure I shall think you do not use me with that affability as in discretion you ought to use me, look you, being as good a man as yourself, both in the disciplines of war, and in the derivation of my birth, and in other particularities.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneIII_11.2/p@70769/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
